---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Container from '../components/ui/Container.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About GVibeDev"
  description="GVibeDev is a personal workshop for games, tools, stories and experiments — built through iteration, testing, curiosity and human-directed use of AI."
>
  <div class="about-page">
    <section class="about-hero">
      <Container>
        <div class="about-hero__grid">
          <div class="about-hero__copy">
            <span class="eyebrow">About GVibeDev</span>
            <h1>A personal workshop for games, tools, stories and experiments.</h1>
            <p class="lead">
              GVibeDev is the name I use for a personal workshop built around one simple idea:
              new tools can let people attempt things that once required skills, teams or resources
              they did not have access to.
            </p>
            <p>
              It is not a software company, not an agency and not a brand dressed up as a team.
              The work begins with ideas, requirements and a willingness to learn whatever the next
              problem demands.
            </p>
            <div class="about-actions">
              <a href="/projects/" class="button button--primary">Explore projects</a>
              <a href="/contact/" class="button button--secondary">Contact</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <aside class="about-hero__panel">
            <span>Working ground</span>
            <strong>Built by making real things.</strong>
            <p>
              The projects collected here move across game design, playable prototypes, editorial
              work, worldbuilding, browser tools and independent technical experimentation.
            </p>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>

    <section class="section-block">
      <Container>
        <div class="two-column">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <span class="eyebrow">Background</span>
            <h2>Learning by building, not by pretending to already know.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="prose-block">
            <p>
              GVibeDev grows out of multidisciplinary interests: writing, game design,
              systems-thinking, visual experimentation and the practical challenge of turning
              ambitious ideas into working artefacts.
            </p>
            <p>
              I do not approach this work by presenting myself as a traditional software engineer.
              Much of the technical side has been learned inside real projects, through iteration,
              debugging, correction, comparison and the discipline of testing whether something
              actually works outside the excitement of the first draft.
            </p>
            <p>
              That is why the portfolio matters. It is not a list of concepts. It is a record of
              attempts that became interfaces, tools, pages, game systems, documents and workflows.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>

    <section class="section-block section-block--deep">
      <Container>
        <div class="two-column two-column--wide-gap">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <span class="eyebrow">Tools, method, responsibility</span>
            <h2>AI is leverage, not autopilot.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="prose-block">
            <p>
              Language models can help write code, analyse systems, research a problem, reorganise a
              text, compare alternatives or accelerate prototyping. They can extend reach, but they
              do not inherit responsibility.
            </p>
            <p>
              Intent, requirements, judgement, verification, acceptance criteria and final direction
              remain human responsibilities. The more powerful the tool becomes, the more important
              the method becomes. Fast generation without verification only produces mistakes faster.
            </p>
            <p>
              That distinction matters here. The goal is not to remove the person from the process,
              but to give one person access to capabilities that previously demanded much larger
              amounts of time, specialised knowledge or external structure.
            </p>
            <blockquote>
              AI can amplify a process. It does not replace the need for clarity, discipline or
              responsibility.
            </blockquote>
            <p>
              This approach eventually became a project of its own: <em>Manuale LLM</em>, a practical
              attempt to turn long experimentation with language models into a repeatable method
              grounded in structure, responsibility and deliberate use.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>

    <section class="section-block">
      <Container>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-card__copy">
            <span class="eyebrow">Featured method project</span>
            <h2>Manuale LLM</h2>
            <p>
              A public writing / method project focused on how to work with language models using
              structure, prompting discipline, iterative diagnosis and human responsibility rather
              than vague automation myths.
            </p>
            <div class="feature-card__actions">
              <a href="/projects/manuale-llm/" class="button button--primary">Open project page</a>
              <a href="https://github.com/GVibeDev/Manuale_LLM" class="button button--secondary">Repository</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <figure class="feature-card__media">
            <img
              src="/assets/projects/manuale-llm/cover.webp"
              alt="Cover of Manuale LLM: Metodo, struttura e responsabilità nel lavoro con modelli linguistici generativi."
              width="601"
              height="902"
              loading="lazy"
              decoding="async"
            />
          </figure>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>

    <section class="section-block section-block--deep">
      <Container>
        <div class="two-column">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <span class="eyebrow">A small shared workbench</span>
            <h2>Some corners of the workshop are shared.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="prose-block">
            <p>
              My son sometimes joins me in experimenting with games, mechanics and wonderfully
              unreasonable ideas. His own public-facing projects live under the <strong>BiggityKot</strong>
              name, with their own tone and identity inside the wider site.
            </p>
            <p>
              Working together is less about teaching a predefined formula and more about discovering
              what happens when curiosity is given tools.
            </p>
            <p>
              The result is not a company-within-a-company, but a shared creative bench where related
              experiments can grow without losing their own personality.
            </p>
            <p>
              <a href="/#biggitykot" class="inline-link">Explore BiggityKot →</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>

    <section class="section-block">
      <Container>
        <div class="closing-grid">
          <article>
            <span class="eyebrow">What this site is for</span>
            <h3>A public record of practice.</h3>
            <p>
              GVibeDev exists to show the work itself: what is being built, how it evolves and what
              becomes possible when strong intent is paired with better tools.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span class="eyebrow">How to reach out</span>
            <h3>Projects, questions, strange ideas.</h3>
            <p>
              For project discussions, repository issues, collaborations or general messages, the
              best next step is the contact page.
            </p>
            <p><a href="/contact/" class="inline-link">Go to Contact →</a></p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </Container>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-page { color: var(--color-text); background: var(--color-bg); }
  .section-block { padding-block: var(--section-space); }
  .section-block--deep { background: var(--color-bg-deep); border-block: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-blue-soft);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: .72rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .about-hero {
    padding-block: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 5rem) clamp(3rem, 7vw, 6rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-bg-deep);
  }
  .about-hero__grid, .two-column, .feature-card, .closing-grid { display: grid; gap: 2rem; }
  .about-hero__copy, .section-heading, .prose-block, .feature-card__copy, .closing-grid article {
    display: grid; gap: 1rem;
  }
  .about-hero h1, .section-heading h2 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 5.8rem);
    line-height: .95;
    letter-spacing: -.055em;
  }
  .section-heading h2 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 4rem); }
  .lead {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1rem + .4vw, 1.35rem);
    line-height: 1.68;
  }
  .about-hero p, .prose-block p, .feature-card__copy p, .closing-grid p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .about-actions, .feature-card__actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .8rem; margin-top: .5rem; }
  .button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 2.8rem;
    padding: .8rem 1.05rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: .78rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    transition: transform .2s ease, border-color .2s ease, background-color .2s ease;
  }
  .button:hover { transform: translateY(-1px); }
  .button--primary {
    color: #08111e;
    background: var(--color-blue-soft);
    border-color: var(--color-blue-soft);
  }
  .button--secondary {
    color: var(--color-text);
    background: var(--color-surface-1);
  }
  .about-hero__panel, .closing-grid article {
    padding: 1.15rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: var(--color-surface-1);
  }
  .about-hero__panel { display: grid; gap: .75rem; align-content: start; }
  .about-hero__panel span { color: var(--color-blue-soft); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .about-hero__panel strong, .closing-grid h3 { font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .closing-grid h3 { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text); }
  .prose-block blockquote {
    margin: .35rem 0;
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-blue-soft);
    background: var(--color-surface-1);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .feature-card {
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 2vw, 1.8rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(25, 36, 56, 0.95), rgba(10, 14, 22, 0.98));
  }
  .feature-card__media {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 18rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-strong);
    background: #02060e;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .feature-card__media img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .inline-link {
    color: var(--color-blue-soft);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .inline-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (min-width: 60rem) {
    .about-hero__grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(18rem, .55fr); gap: 4rem; align-items: end; }
    .two-column { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr); gap: 4rem; align-items: start; }
    .two-column--wide-gap { gap: 5rem; }
    .feature-card { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 18rem; gap: 3rem; align-items: center; }
    .closing-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }
</style>
